// Everyday words (V2.1 §10.4; H10): what anyone of a forager band may say when a language model
// phrases its speech acts — the small words of every sentence, people and kin, the body, feelings
// and the mind, what one does, the land and what lives on it, the things of a camp, what things
// are like, time and place, greetings. A phrased line holds only words its speaker may say: these,
// the words of the techniques it knows (`techniques.ron`), the names it knows and its language's
// glosses. Words are plain forms; the filter reads -s, -ed, -ing, -er, -est, -ly and -ness onto
// them, and irregular forms are listed as words of their own. Kept to what a forager knows: no
// metal, farming, writing, money or later things (`later_ages.ron`), and no compass points (a
// line says "there", not a direction the speaker does not know).
(
    schema: 1,
    entries: [
        (
            id: "function_words",
            name: "The small words of every sentence",
            status: Implemented,
            words: [
                // Pronouns.
